  html += '<p class="lede"><strong>Bottom line:</strong> Job Board really is the top source by volume. But it turns the smallest share of its candidates into hires. Sending it more candidates without fixing that first will not help.</p>';

  html += '<h3 class="section-title">Answer to Question 2</h3>';
  html += '<div class="summary-grid">';
  html += statCard(
    'Acceptance rate, counting "undecided" as a no',
    pFail['Rate (%)'] + '%',
    `Based on ${pFail['Total counted']} offers. Likely range: ${pFail['95% likely range']} — see the Glossary.`
  );
  html += statCard(
    'Acceptance rate, leaving "undecided" out',
    pExcl['Rate (%)'] + '%',
    `Based on ${pExcl['Total counted']} offers. Likely range: ${pExcl['95% likely range']}.`
  );
  html += '</div>';
  html += '<p class="lede"><strong>Bottom line:</strong> these two ranges overlap. With only 36 offers total, we cannot say which number is more correct. See "Acceptance rate, two ways to count it" in the menu, and the metric spec in the roadmap doc for the fix.</p>';

  html += '<h3 class="section-title">Two problems nobody asked about</h3>';
  html += '<div class="summary-grid">';
  html += statCard(
    'Open job requisitions that are overdue',
    overdue.length + ' of ' + open.length,
    'Past their own target close date, some by over a year. The largest single problem found in this data.',
    true
  );
  html += statCard(
    'One interviewer whose calls don\'t match the outcome',
    'Rakesh Sethi',
    `Told ${noHireCount} of his ${rakesh['Total interviews given']} candidates "no" or "strong no." 9 of them were hired anyway, or are still in the running.`,
    true
  );
  html += '</div>';

  html += '<h3 class="section-title">How much of the data has an error</h3>';
  html += '<div class="summary-grid">';
  html += statCard(
    'Records affected by a data problem',
    mat['Records affected'] + ' of ' + mat['Total records in that table (or in the whole dataset for the last row)'],
    `${mat['Share affected (%)']}% of everything pulled. Small in total, but concentrated in the records both questions above depend on.`
  );
  html += '</div>';

  html += '<h3 class="section-title">Where to read more</h3><p class="lede">Use the menu on the left for the full table behind any number above. The complete write-up is in two files: <code>docs/strategy/talentflow-q3-roadmap.md</code> (what to build, what not to build, and why) and <code>docs/discovery/talentflow-data-quality-audit.md</code> (every data problem found).</p>';
  return html;
}

